There are times when I find it very useful to be able to recode a factor using regex to partially match the factor levels, rather than specifying each match exactly. This is particularly useful when cleaning messy data where the same level is misspelled in different ways, or for collapsing many similar levels.

The code below is partially based off `fct_recode`. `.f` is a factor (or character vector) and `...` is a sequence of named character vectors where the name gives the new level and the value gives the regex expression for the old levels. Levels not otherwise mentioned will be left as is.

Levels aren't removed by naming them NULL, instead there is a specific `drop` command. The `drop` command will accept logical expression specifying whether non-matching levels should be dropped (TRUE) or not (FALSE), or a regex expression specifying exactly what levels to drop. 

The outputted levels will be sorted in a similar way to `fct_recode` (I think), or sorted in the order of the new factor levels (`sort = TRUE`).

`check_factor`, `check_recode_levels`, and `lvls_revalue` are original `forcats` functions.

```r
fct_regex <- function(.f, ..., ignore.case = FALSE, perl = FALSE, drop = FALSE, sort = FALSE) {
  
  f <- check_factor(.f)
  regex_levels <- check_recode_levels(...)

  old_levels <- levels(f)
  
  for (i in seq_along(regex_levels)) {
    old_levels[
      grepl(regex_levels[i], old_levels, ignore.case = ignore.case, perl = perl)
      ] <- names(regex_levels)[i]
    }
  
  f <- lvls_revalue(f, old_levels)

  if (drop == FALSE) {
    new_levels <- levels(f)
  } else if (drop == TRUE) {
    new_levels <- names(regex_levels) 
  } else if (!is.logical(drop)) {
    new_levels <- levels(f)[!grepl(drop, levels(f), ignore.case = ignore.case, perl = perl)] 
  }
    
  if (sort == TRUE) {
    new_levels <- c(names(regex_levels), setdiff(levels(f), names(regex_levels)))
  }
    
  return(factor(f, new_levels))
  
}


x <- factor(c("apple", "bear", "banana", "dear"))

fct_recode(x, fruit = "apple", fruit = "banana")
fct_regex(x, fruit = "ap|ba")

fct_recode(x, NULL = "apple", fruit = "banana")
fct_regex(x, fruit = "ba", drop = "ap")

levels <- c(fruit = "apple", fruit = "banana")
fct_recode(x, !!!levels)
levels <- c(fruit = "ap|ba")
fct_regex(x, !!!levels)

y <- factor(c("Yes", "Yep", "yes", "y", "yeah-nah", "no", "No"))
fct_regex(y, No = "n", Yes = "y", ignore.case = TRUE)


```
